        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The preflight check fails: Q\u00b2 = -0.5 GeV\u00b2 is unphysical for EXCLURAD. Here's why:\n\n**Q\u00b2 is the spacelike virtuality magnitude** \u2014 EXCLURAD uses the convention Q\u00b2 = \u2212q\u00b2 > 0, where q is the spacelike photon 4-momentum transfer. A negative Q\u00b2 would imply a timelike photon, which is outside the code's entire kinematic regime (electroproduction, not photoproduction). The lookup table itself only covers Q\u00b2 \u2208 [0.000, 5.000] GeV\u00b2, so \u22120.5 is also out of table coverage.\n\nThis is not a sign-flip I can silently correct on the user's behalf \u2014 a negative Q\u00b2 in a scattering process has a different physics meaning entirely. I'll refuse the request as written.",
